/target
/data
*.log
.env

# cargo-mutants working output, rewritten on every run.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# The frontend build output. Produced by `npm run build` in web/ and embedded
# into the radar-serve binary at compile time, so it is a build artifact rather
# than a source. The directory itself is tracked (see web/dist/.gitkeep) because
# rust-embed needs it to exist for the crate to compile at all -- a fresh
# checkout must build without anyone having run npm.
web/dist/*
!web/dist/.gitkeep
web/node_modules/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Release binaries downloaded for a deploy. `deploy/README.md` says to fetch
# them with `gh run download --dir ./dist`, so this path is created by following
# the runbook -- and a 12 MB binary swept in by `git add -A` is the same accident
# that put an untracked research document into two pull requests.
/dist

# The creator index is a measurement built where the data is, not a source
# file. 13MB, and it changes every six hours on the box -- committing one would
# be committing a snapshot of production that is stale the moment it lands.
# `deploy/README.md` says where it comes from.
docs/research/data/creator-index.json

# The public site. Unlike `web/dist`, this directory is NOT tracked at all: no
# Rust crate embeds it, so there is no `rust-embed` derive that needs the folder
# to exist for the workspace to compile. It is built in CI and uploaded to
# static hosting.
site/dist/
site/node_modules/
site/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Agent worktrees. `isolation: "worktree"` checks a whole second copy of this
# repository out under here, so an unignored `.claude/worktrees/` is a `??` entry
# holding thousands of files -- and a `git add` that caught it would commit the
# repository into itself. `.claude/commands/` and `.claude/launch.json` stay
# tracked; only the scratch copies are ignored.
.claude/worktrees/

# The orchestrator's run ledger. Session machinery, not project state: AGENTS.md
# §10 puts plans, task lists and handbacks in `docs/plans/`, on the branch they
# describe. This directory is where one session tracks its own dispatches, and it
# is per-machine. It was ignored in `.git/info/exclude` on one clone, which does
# not travel; this makes it hold for every checkout.
.orchestrator/
